  - id: "JOURNAL-041"
    date: "2026-05-24"
    mode: "STANDARD"
    hot_entries_consulted: ["VAC-004", "PAT-003", "PAT-012"]
    l0_abstract: "Eliminated the remaining Graphify hook broken-pipe recurrence path across active Gemini and Graphify templates."
    pourquoi: "The project Codex hook already consumed stdin, but two installed Graphify Gemini templates and the global Gemini trusted hook registry still used an echo-only allow command. A hook command that can exit without reading stdin recreates the same BeforeToolUse broken-pipe failure after reinstall or in another agent host, so the safe contract is now stdin consumption before any allow response."
    validations:
      - "project .codex/hooks.json: PreToolUse command consumes stdin and simulation exits 0 with empty stdout/stderr"
      - "Graphify templates patched in user site-packages and pipx site-packages"
      - "global ~/.gemini/trusted_hooks.json graphify command consumes stdin and returns JSON allow"
      - "graphify codex install regenerated a stdin-safe project PreToolUse hook"
      - "legacy echo-only Gemini allow command scan: no matches in active Graphify/Gemini surfaces"
      - "scribe doctor --suggest-fix before edit: 0 errors, 5 legacy warnings"
    scribe_delta: "VAC-004 | JOURNAL-041"
  - id: "JOURNAL-042"
    date: "2026-05-24"
    mode: "STANDARD"
    hot_entries_consulted: ["VAC-004", "JOURNAL-041", "PAT-012"]
    l0_abstract: "Engraved the Graphify upstream reinstall caveat into the portable SCRIBE bundle rules."
    pourquoi: "The local Broken pipe fix is only production-complete if future agents remember that an upstream Graphify reinstall can overwrite patched templates. Putting the caveat in the bundle README and AGENTS rules makes the recurrence guard travel with the reusable SCRIBE/TENOR workflow instead of living only in one session transcript."
    validations:
      - "bundle README points future agents to Graphify hook hardening rules"
      - "bundle docs/AGENTS.md states Graphify reinstall/upgrade is a recurrence risk until stdin-consuming templates are reverified"
      - "bundle docs/AGENTS.md requires Codex and Gemini hook simulation after Graphify reinstall or upgrade"
    scribe_delta: "JOURNAL-042"
  - id: "JOURNAL-043"
    date: "2026-05-24"
    mode: "STANDARD"
    hot_entries_consulted: ["VAC-004", "JOURNAL-041", "JOURNAL-042", "PAT-012", "PAT-022"]
    l0_abstract: "Added an executable Graphify hook guard and upstreamable patch to the SCRIBE bundle."
    pourquoi: "The remaining production gap was that a future Graphify reinstall from upstream could overwrite local site-packages edits. A bundle command, patch file, generated-agent instruction, and unit tests make the fix discoverable, repeatable, and enforceable by future LLM agents even without relying on session memory."
    validations:
      - "scribe graphify-hooks: PASS on active installed templates and hooks"
      - "unittest discover: 37 tests passed, including Graphify hook guard apply/no-apply coverage"
      - "py_compile: bundle CLI, guard script, template script, and new tests compiled"
      - "scribe install .: regenerated AGENTS.md with graphify-hooks guidance"
      - "scribe doctor --suggest-fix: 0 errors, 5 legacy warnings"
