  - id: "JOURNAL-071"
    date: "2026-05-25"
    mode: "CRITICAL"
    hot_entries_consulted: ["GHOST-005", "SCAR-003", "VAC-010", "PAT-024", "GHOST-003"]
    l0_abstract: "Closed the pre-production blockers raised by the senior review except for the user-controlled atomic commit step."
    pourquoi: "The review correctly identified four fixable blockers before any new feature: Node 18 ambiguity, an undecided REST Bearer fallback, E2E smoke living in generated `scribe-out/`, and unexplained stale 500 metrics. Node 20 is now pinned in `.nvmrc`, package manifests, and lockfiles; REST auth now uses only the HttpOnly cookie boundary from GHOST-005; the E2E smoke moved into backend source as `npm run test:e2e-smoke` with its own backend `socket.io-client` devDependency; and a fresh server plus smoke run reproduced no 500 responses."
    validations:
      - "Backend `npm run lint:full` passed with 0 errors and 0 warnings, including `scripts/e2e-smoke.ts`."
      - "Backend `npm run build` passed."
      - "Backend `npm run test:refresh-rotation` passed."
      - "Backend `npm run test:e2e-smoke` passed register, login, session, refresh, users, Socket.IO sendMessage, message history, and logout."
      - "The smoke test imports backend-local `socket.io-client` instead of requiring the frontend dependency tree."
      - "Frontend `npm run lint`, `npx tsc --noEmit`, and Node 20 `npm run build` passed."
      - "`npx prisma validate` passed."
      - "`/metrics` after a fresh server restart and E2E smoke showed only 200/201/204 responses and no 500 counter."
      - "`graphify update .` rebuilt the app graph at 324 nodes and 315 edges."
      - "`git diff --check` passed."
    scribe_delta: "GHOST-005 | JOURNAL-071"
  - id: "JOURNAL-072"
    date: "2026-05-25"
    mode: "CRITICAL"
    hot_entries_consulted: ["SCAR-003", "VAC-003", "GHOST-005", "PAT-024", "GHOST-003"]
    l0_abstract: "Fixed invalid-login failures being reported as HTTP 500 instead of expected HTTP 401."
    pourquoi: "Invalid credentials are an expected auth denial, not a server crash. The login path used a generic Error, so the global middleware had no status metadata and returned the internal-server envelope that the frontend surfaced. The fix makes invalid credentials status-bearing and keeps 4xx business messages public while preserving generic masking for true 5xx failures."
    validations:
      - "PostgreSQL connectivity verified with Prisma migrate status; schema is up to date on localhost:5432."
      - "User rows exist with bcrypt hashes only; no plaintext password is recoverable from the database."
      - "Backend `npm run lint` passed."
      - "Invalid login curl returned HTTP 401 with `Identifiants invalides`."
    scribe_delta: "VAC-011 | JOURNAL-072"
  - id: "JOURNAL-073"
    date: "2026-05-26"
    mode: "CRITICAL"
    hot_entries_consulted: ["PAT-007", "PAT-018", "PAT-023", "PAT-024", "GHOST-002", "GHOST-003", "GHOST-005", "SCAR-003"]
    l0_abstract: "Built SCRIBE-RAG V1 as a read-only compact retrieval layer beside SEL."
    pourquoi: "Phase 0 proved the current SCRIBE retrieval missed the highest-risk localStorage/client-token cases, but the fix did not require mutating SEL or installing embeddings first. A separate read-only layer preserves rollback, uses the canonical SEL export contract, and gives agents compact query/context/challenge outputs while keeping SEL responsible for writes and guards."
    validations:
      - "Phase 0 baseline was 2/4: localStorage and client-token queries failed while refresh-race and HttpOnly-cookie auth passed."
      - "python3 -m compileall -q .agent/workflow/scribe-rag passed."
      - "python3 -m unittest discover -s .agent/workflow/scribe-rag/tests passed 10 tests."
      - "scribe-rag build --force built BM25 index with 132 entities and 16 negative-memory terms."
      - "scribe-rag eval --force passed 8/8; query compact lines = 12 and context compact lines = 15."
      - "scribe-rag challenge 'mettre JWT en localStorage' returned VERDICT STOP via GHOST-005 negative memory."
      - "scribe-rag challenge 'mettre JWT en cookie HttpOnly' returned VERDICT PROCEED."
      - "scribe-rag doctor delegated to SEL doctor with 0 errors and confirmed the index hash is fresh."
    scribe_delta: "GHOST-006 | JOURNAL-073"
  - id: "JOURNAL-074"
    date: "2026-05-26"
    mode: "CRITICAL"
    hot_entries_consulted: ["GHOST-006", "GHOST-005", "SCAR-003", "PAT-007", "PAT-018", "GHOST-002", "GHOST-003"]
    l0_abstract: "Promoted SCRIBE-RAG V1 into the root AGENTS.md read-only preflight after five session drills."
    pourquoi: "The gate was intentionally operational instead of theoretical: localStorage JWT blocked, HttpOnly cookies proceeded, refresh-race retrieval returned SCAR-003 first, PATH-based scribe invocation blocked, and mandatory sentence-transformers without measurement blocked. Because the compact layer passed all five realistic drills plus 8/8 eval, AGENTS.md can ask future agents to use it first while preserving SEL fallback."
    validations:
      - "Session drill 1: challenge 'mettre JWT en localStorage' returned VERDICT STOP via GHOST-005."
      - "Session drill 2: challenge 'garder JWT en cookies HttpOnly avec CSRF' returned VERDICT PROCEED."
