    mode: "CRITICAL"
    hot_entries_consulted: ["GHOST-006", "GHOST-005", "SCAR-003", "VAC-011", "PAT-024", "GHOST-003"]
    l0_abstract: "Activated scribe-rag BM25 as the primary preflight and benchmarked SEL, BM25, and Hybrid with real command outputs."
    pourquoi: >
      Governance moved from intuition to measured data. scribe-rag is now the primary read-only preflight in AGENTS.md, but the benchmark shows the default must be BM25, not Hybrid: BM25 consumes fewer query words than SEL, finds all four semantic cases in top-3, blocks localStorage JWT correctly, and avoids the heavy model dependency. SEL remains required for doctor, lock, state, writes, guards, and as fallback authority.
    validations:
      - "AGENTS.md now defines scribe-rag as the primary read-only preflight with STOP/REVIEW/PROCEED challenge semantics."
      - "sentence-transformers is installed at version 5.5.1; all-MiniLM-L6-v2 returned OK: 384 dims."
      - "scribe-rag build --with-embeddings --force returned mode hybrid, entities 136, negative_terms 21, dimension 384."
      - "Benchmark output sizes: SEL context 18/170, BM25 context 15/155, Hybrid context 15/154; SEL query 34/221, BM25 query 12/125, Hybrid query 12/131."
      - "Benchmark times: SEL context 0.096308s, BM25 context 0.130306s, Hybrid context 17.628567s; SEL query 0.396621s, BM25 query 0.126069s, Hybrid query 21.760626s."
      - "Semantic retrieval top-3: SEL 2/4, BM25 4/4, Hybrid 4/4; top-1: SEL 0/4, BM25 2/4, Hybrid 3/4."
      - "Challenge localStorage JWT: SEL WARN, BM25 STOP, Hybrid STOP. Challenge cookies HttpOnly refresh rotation: SEL BLOCK, BM25 REVIEW, Hybrid REVIEW."
      - "Portability measurements: SEL bundle 2.0M, scribe-rag bundle 168K, model cache 168M; empty bootstrap command returned rc=1 because Graphify is absent in an empty project, then BM25 build succeeded in 0.627816s and Hybrid build succeeded in 27.512511s."
    scribe_delta: "GHOST-007 | JOURNAL-076 | AGENTS.md preflight V3"
  - id: "JOURNAL-077"
    date: "2026-05-26"
    mode: "CRITICAL"
    hot_entries_consulted: ["GHOST-007", "GHOST-006", "GHOST-005", "SCAR-003", "PAT-024", "GHOST-003"]
    l0_abstract: "Closed the two pre-commit blockers for BM25 canonical rollout."
    pourquoi: >
      The benchmark decision was valid, but two operational defects would hurt future agents: empty-project bootstrap returned rc=1 and a junior agent would treat that as a real failure, while an approved cookie/CSRF/refresh plan returned REVIEW because refresh synonyms pulled in SCAR-003 race-condition memory. The fix makes empty projects create an informational Graphify placeholder with rc=0, keeps rc=1 when application code exists without a valid graph, tightens negative-memory matching for long rejected phrases, and adds an approved security pattern so safe cookie-refresh plans proceed without weakening STOP for localStorage JWT.
    validations:
      - "Bootstrap empty project now returns rc=0 with Graphify placeholder info."
      - "Bootstrap project with application marker and missing Graphify returns rc=1 with explicit Graphify error."
      - "scribe-rag challenge 'cookies HttpOnly refresh rotation' returns PROCEED."
      - "scribe-rag challenge 'mettre JWT en localStorage' remains STOP."
      - "scribe-rag challenge 'corriger bootstrap projet vide pour BM25 canonique' no longer returns STOP from generic negative-memory overlap."
      - "Unit tests cover empty-project Graphify placeholder, app-code Graphify error, approved cookie refresh challenge, and generic empty-project overlap."
    scribe_delta: "PAT-027 | JOURNAL-077 | bootstrap rc policy | challenge false-positive fix"
